  "description": "MEHFOY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C34 H80 F9 N18 Nd4 O18 3+,3(C2 F3 O2 1-),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.872-4.042 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.75-111.61°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C40H82N18O25F18Nd4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
